 ref←GetRefToAPLGit2 dummy
⍝ Returns the ref user commands are supposed to execute their code in: the project itself when
⍝ it is open and `DEVELOPMENT` is set in `⎕SE.APLGit2`, and the installed package otherwise.\\
⍝ Note that both are API namespaces, so `ref.##` gets you to the package itself either way.\\
⍝ This is THE implementation; the identically named method in the user command script is just
⍝ a cover for it, so that the two can never drift apart.
 :If 9=#.⎕NC'APLGit2.APLGit2'
 :AndIf 0<⎕SE.APLGit2.⎕NC'DEVELOPMENT'
 :AndIf ⎕SE.APLGit2.DEVELOPMENT
     ref←#.APLGit2.APLGit2.API
 :Else
     ref←⎕SE.APLGit2
 :EndIf
⍝Done
